infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Field-count vs multiplicative complexity scoring
  desc Same query, same 1000-cost budget — only one formula sees the row explosion
  compares
    - label Field-count rule (under-counts)
      children
        - label Field-count: 1 per field over the AST
          desc Ignores list-argument size entirely
        - label Scores 50 for the query
          desc 10-deep query, 5 fields per level
        - label Sails under the 1000-cost budget
          desc Passes validation, every resolver fires
        - label Query actually reads 10^10 rows
          desc first:100 at 5 levels = 100^5, invisible to the scorer
    - label Multiplicative rule (correct)
      children
        - label Multiplicative: weight + sum(first x child)
          desc Multiplies by each list argument's size
        - label Scores 100^5 for the same query
          desc Surfaces the real row expansion
        - label Astronomically over the 1000 budget
          desc Rejected at AST parse time, zero resolvers fire
        - label Matches GitHub's public formula
          desc A documented version of the multiplicative rule
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
